{{Quote|We would love to visit you on Garel.|The Seventh Sister after discovering a recording revealing the Spectres were hiding on Garel|<ref name="Future of the Force">{{Rebels|The Future of the Force}}</ref>}}
'''Garel''' was a [[planet]] located in the [[Garel system]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]]' [[Lothal sector]] that was controlled by the [[Galactic Empire]]. It was the [[homeworld]] of Imperial [[Supply Master]] [[Yogar Lyste]]. Garel was several [[Standard minute|minutes]] away from the planet [[Lothal]] via [[hyperspace]] travel. Several [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the rebel [[Phoenix Cell]] established a temporary hiding place on Garel. The rebels were forced to move after the Empire discovered their presence and assembled a [[Imperial Navy|fleet]] to [[Battle of Garel|attack them]]. Many years later, individuals such as [[Ushos O. Statura]] fought to [[Liberation of Garel|liberate]] Garel from the yoke of the Galactic Empire.

==Description==
[[File:Garel_City.png|thumb|left|200px|250px|[[Garel City]]'s rock formations]]
Garel was a rocky [[Planet|world]] with dry [[Temperature|temperate]] [[desert]]s<ref name="VE" /> that was located within the [[Lothal sector]] of the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="Droids in Distress" /><ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /><ref name="Dawn" /> It was known for its tall, wind-carved sedimentary rock formations, its purple twilight sky, and its cities built in large craters, such as [[Garel City]].<ref name="Droids in Distress" /><ref name="Dawn" /> Garel served as a major shipping hub within the Lothal sector, though during the [[Imperial Era]] it was also home to several criminal organizations such as the [[Black Sun]] and the [[Broken Horn Syndicate]].<ref name="Dawn" /> Due to its proximity to the planet [[Lothal]], there was a large amount of trade and travel between the two worlds.<ref name="VE" />

==History==
During the reign of the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]], [[Janyor]] of [[Bith (planet)|Bith]] erected a statue to commemorate the [[4 BBY|fifteen year anniversary]] of the end of the [[Clone Wars]]; the statue was considered scandalously critical of the Empire and was torn down some [[Standard year|years]] later.<ref name="Dawn" /><ref name="HoloNetNews">{{HoloNetNewsTumblr|post/96732887451/holonet-news-special-report-controversial-statue|text=Special Report: Controversial Statue Finally Destroyed|int=HoloNet News Special Report: Controversial Statue Finally Destroyed}}</ref> A small group staged an impromptu [[Garel statue protest|protest]], but was quelled by local authorities. According to the Imperial [[propaganda]] announcer [[Alton Kastle]], the official reason behind the statue's destruction was a belief by the [[Coalition for Progress]] division of [[Commission for the Preservation of the New Order|COMPNOR]] that the statue was a danger to the public.<ref name="HoloNetNews" /> The Imperial reaction spurred many citizens to sympathize with or join [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|dissident movements]].<ref name="Dawn" />

[[File:Garel_City_Spaceport.png|thumb|right|250px|The Spectres took a job on Garel]]
After joining the [[Spectres|crew]] of the ''[[Ghost]]'', [[Ezra Bridger]] and his new rebel "family" accepted a job from the [[Devaronian]] crime lord [[Cikatro Vizago]] to steal a shipment of Imperial [[T-7 ion disruptor rifle]]s from a warehouse in [[Garel City Spaceport]]. While picking up the rifles, they were pursued by Imperial forces led by the Imperial [[Minister]] [[Maketh Tua]], who wanted to mass produce them on Lothal. During their trip to Garel, the rebels also picked up two hitchhikers, the [[droid]]s [[C-3PO]] and [[R2-D2]], who had been sent by the [[Alderaan]]ian [[Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] to prevent the rifles from falling into the hands of the Empire. After escaping Garel, they managed to destroy the rifles during a [[Mission to steal Imperial weapons#Battle on Lothal|skirmish]] with Imperial forces on Lothal.<ref name="Droids in Distress" />

Following an Imperial crackdown in response to the Lothal insurgency, the [[slicer]] [[Merei Spanjaf]], [[Spanjaf family|her family]], the [[Leonis family]], the [[nanny droid]] [[Auntie Nags]], and the poet [[Holshef]] fled to Garel with the help of the [[Ithorian]] bartender [[Jho|Old Jho]] and the crew of the ''Ghost''. Later, they were joined by [[Zare Leonis]] and his sister [[Dhara Leonis|Dhara]], who had been [[Rescue of Dhara Leonis|rescued]] from the [[Arkanis Academy|Arkanis Imperial Academy]]. Merei's father [[Gandr Spanjaf|Gandr]] created false identities for both his family and the Leonises.<ref name="Secret Academy">''[[Servants of the Empire: The Secret Academy]]''</ref>

After the destruction of [[Phoenix Cell]]'s flagship, ''[[Phoenix Home]]'', the rebels set up a presence on Garel and hid in the planet's sprawling [[spaceport]]s.<ref name="Brothers of the Broken Horn">{{Rebels|Brothers of the Broken Horn}}</ref> By this stage, the crew of the ''Ghost'' had joined Phoenix Squadron, which was part of a wider rebel network.<ref name="Fire Across the Galaxy">{{Rebels|Fire Across the Galaxy}}</ref> During a mission to scavenge fuel cells for the planet [[Rinn]], which was experiencing an energy crisis, [[Commander]] [[Jun Sato]] sent the crew of the ''Ghost'' to search the streets of [[Garel City]] for fuel cells. However, Ezra and the astromech droid [[C1-10P|Chopper]] managed to obtained five power generators during an unauthorized mission to rescue Vizago.<ref name="Brothers of the Broken Horn" />

Later, the new [[Phoenix Leader]], [[Hera Syndulla]], dispatched two Phoenix cell members to pick up [[starfighter]] parts from the marketplace in Garel City. She also sent [[Sabine Wren]], along with Ezra and Chopper, on a mission to Garel City Spaceport to pick up a mysterious courier and transport him offworld to [[Havoc Outpost]]. This mysterious courier turned out to be the [[GNK-series power droid]] [[EG-86]], who was carrying information vital to the rebel network. Before the crew of the ''Ghost'' could pick up EG-86, they were cornered by the [[Black Sun]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Ketsu Onyo]], who was a former acquaintance of Sabine. Following a skirmish with Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s, Sabine and Chopper managed to flee into space but were pursued by Ketsu. After an [[Arquitens-class command cruiser|''Arquitens''-class command cruiser]] arrived, Sabine joined forces with her former adversary to transport EG-86 to Havoc Outpost.<ref name="Blood Sisters">{{Rebels|Blood Sisters}}</ref>

After Ezra and Commander Sato were captured by an [[Interdictor (Interdictor-class)|Imperial Interdictor]] in the [[Del Zennis system]], [[Garazeb Orrelios]] ambushed two stormtroopers. The rebels stripped off their [[Stormtrooper armor|armor]], which was used during a successful mission to rescue their rebel comrades from the Imperial Interdictor.<ref name="Stealth Strike">{{Rebels|Stealth Strike}}</ref> Later, the former [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] visited her rebel allies [[Kanan Jarrus]] and Ezra on Garel to enlist their support for a mission to investigate the [[Inquisitorius|Inquisitors]]' secondary mission, which they subsequently learned involved kidnapping [[Force-sensitive]] children. While on [[Takobo]], Ezra accidentally revealed to one of the [[Seventh Sister]]'s [[ID9 seeker droid]]s that the Phoenix rebels were hiding on Garel.<ref name="Future of the Force" />

[[File:GhostDestroysTractorBeam-Rebels-Legacy.png|thumb|left|250px|Rebel forces would be driven off Garel]]
Using this information, Imperial forces based on [[Lothal]] launched an [[Battle of Garel|assault]] on Garel in order to crush the Phoenix rebels. Imperial stormtroopers in Garel City also took part in the assault. After fighting Imperial ground forces, the crew of the ''Ghost'' and several rebel ships managed to take off but were immediately fired upon by the Imperial fleet, which included several [[Star Destroyer]]s and [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter|TIE fighters]]. At least one of the Phoenix Cell's ships was shot down and crashed onto the streets of Garel City. Several Imperial laser blasts also hit civilian targets on Garel City.<ref name="Legacy">{{Rebels|Legacy (episode)}}</ref>

During the assault, [[Admiral]] [[Kassius Konstantine]]'s Star Destroyer ''[[Relentless]]'' caught Commander Sato's [[CR90 corvette]] in a [[tractor beam projector]]. However, Hera used the ''Ghost'' to knock out the tractor beam, allowing Sato and the rest of the Phoenix fleet to jump into hyperspace. Meanwhile Ezra, along with Kanan and Chopper, departed on the ''Ghost''{{'s}} auxiliary shuttle the ''[[Phantom]]'' for Lothal to find his parents [[Ephraim Bridger|Ephraim]] and [[Mira Bridger]].<ref name="Legacy" />

Some [[time]] before the [[Cyrkon Extraction]], the [[smuggler]]s [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]] worked with [[Akko]] and his gang in a scam on Garel.<ref name="Age of Rebellion - Han Solo">[[Age of Rebellion - Han Solo 1|''Age of Rebellion - Han Solo'' 1]]</ref>

Garel would maintain an Imperial presence in the form of an [[Imperial Complex (Garel)|Imperial Complex]]. A [[munitions factory]] was opened there<ref name="Bounty Hunters 24" /> between [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]],<ref name="BH 24 Date">The events of [[Bounty Hunters 24|''Bounty Hunters'' 24]], including the [[death]] of Skarhorn on [[Garel]], take place after the [[Escape from Cloud City]] and before the [[Rescue of Han Solo]], which are dated to [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]], respectively, by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''.</ref>

[[Ushos O. Statura]] was born on Garel and, when he was a teenager, [[Liberation of Garel|fought]] to free the planet from the Empire's oppression.<ref name="Databank Statura" />

==Behind the scenes==
Garel first appeared as a hologram in "[[HoloNet News Special Report: Controversial Statue Finally Destroyed]]", the fourth in a series of exclusive Holonetnews.com videos related to the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'',<ref name="HoloNetNews" /> which was first published on September 5, 2014.<ref name="Date">{{JCFCite|url=posts/post-51801950|board=Star Wars Television|thread=Imperial HoloNet News|user=Barriss_Coffee|date=2014-09-05|time=3:23 PM|archivedate=20150920225715}}</ref>

